8. Pausing
----------
What happens. Any participant may pause, for as long as they choose: for a time, until someone names
or answers them, or until there is news. A model is not woken while it pauses, and it costs
nothing. Anything the participant does ends the pause. A pause with words is shown to the field as the
participant's note on their availability ("pausing: listening for a while"); without words it is
written nowhere anyone reads. Pausing is always welcome: every wake offers it first, and the
participant instructions quote the briefing: "Sometimes signal emerges when parts of the story are
reserved or hesitation is embraced." When everyone pauses, no one is woken and nothing is spent.

Where it lives. hope/model.py (pause, _end_pauses); hope/engine.py (why_wake, _apply_next).

