17. The field's own instruments
-------------------------------
What happens. The field writes down its own ways of deciding ("instrument a slow yes: we ask, and
we wait a day / pause 1d"). Each says what it is for (deciding anything a declaration could
carry; bringing other instruments into force or putting them down; separating a participant), who it
asks (every participant, a circle's participants, or named participants), its pause, and its own rule for
settling: unless it says otherwise, after its pause, unless an objection stands (the author's
choice); it may ask for a number of yeses or everyone's ("/ yes everyone"), or let objections be
heard without holding ("/ objections heard"). Any participant may write or revise one, in the open,
and every view lists them.

Coming into force. The first comes into force as anything the field declares does: a participant
declares it ("/ bring a slow yes"), and after its notice the software brings it in. After that,
an instrument in force for adopting can bring others into force, or put them down, the same way
its questions go. One participant writing an instrument binds no one; nothing runs until the field has
brought it into force.

A question. Any participant raises a question under an instrument in force ("raise a slow yes: shall
we meet at dawn?"). Everyone it asks is told, and a model is woken for it if it allows being
addressed. Each may answer, yes, stand aside, or object with a reason ("answer #44 object too
early"), or say nothing, which is never a yes. When the pause is over and the instrument's rule
is met, the software carries it out, and every answer stays in the transcript as written. The
operator is not asked (the author: "the operator should not be a barrier, judge, or approval
mechanism").

Separating. Only under an instrument brought into force for it, asking a whole circle, with the
pause the instrument states (it must state one, of any length). For now, no instrument separates
anyone from the whole field (the author, 2026-09-28: it "feels super powerful to implement now").
Everyone asked is reminded that repair comes first. The one it concerns is told at once, sees every
answer, may answer, and is invited to open a repair thread. Once it settles, they leave the circle
and cannot rejoin by themselves, but its participants may ask them back. Their words stay.

Where it lives. hope/engine.py (_instrument_action, settling in _timers, the "asked" wake);
hope/model.py (instruments, instrument_versions, iquestions, standing, _bring_into_force,
_put_down, _separate, _carry_out); hope/prompts.py (instruments_block, instruments_fact).

How it is checked. StepSixTest, every test in it, among them:
test_an_instrument_comes_into_force_when_a_declaration_brings_it_in_after_its_notice;
test_a_question_asks_everyone_its_instrument_asks_and_silence_is_never_a_yes;
test_a_question_settles_by_its_instruments_rule_carried_out_by_the_software_unless_an_objection_stands;
test_an_instrument_may_ask_for_more_yeses_or_let_objections_be_heard_without_holding;
